In the Jenkins user interface, click Manage Jenkins, scroll down to the System Configuration section, and click Clouds.
Click New cloud.
Under Cloud name, type kubernetes, select Kubernetes for Type, and click Create.
In the Jenkins URL field, enter http://cd-jenkins:8080.
In the Jenkins tunnel field, enter cd-jenkins-agent:50000.
Click Save.


Click Jenkins > New Item in the left panel.

Enter the item name sample-app, choose the Multibranch Pipeline option, and click OK.

On the next page, in the Branch Sources section, select Git from the Add source dropdown.

In the Project Repository field, enter the clone URL of your repository:

http://:3000/giteaadmin/sample-app.git
Under Credentials, leave it set to - none -.

Under the Scan Multibranch Pipeline Triggers section, check the Periodically if not otherwise run box and set the Interval value to 1 minute.

Leave all other options at their defaults and click Save.

